<refsynopsisdiv id="dpm_master_server_refresh_config.synopsis">
    <title>Synopsis</title>
    <cmdsynopsis><command>
      dpm_server_refresh_config [ OPTIONS ] filename
</command>
    </cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsect1 id="dpm_master_server_refresh_config.options">
    <title>Arguments</title>
    <para>Accepted arguments:</para>
    <variablelist>
        <varlistentry>
            <term><option>--help</option></term>
            <listitem>
            <para>usage </para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term><option>filename</option></term>
            <listitem>
            <para>dpm.properties configuration file to use </para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term><option>--host host:port</option></term>
            <listitem>
            <para>TCP host and port pair to use to connect to dpm_master_server </para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term><option>--verbose verbosity</option></term>
            <listitem>
            <para>Add program trace information.  Levels of verbosity are TRACE, DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR, FATAL. </para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>

    </variablelist>

</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="dpm_master_server_refresh_config.description">
    <title>Description</title>
    <para>Update dpm_server's configuration with a new or changed properties file.  If no properties file is given, it uses the default.  Note that updates to dpm_master policies are additive only.  Existing policy parameters may not be changed, deleted or replaced, but new ones may be added.</para>
</refsect1>


